# A2 might look like it shifts "contrary". It does not: it holds that temperance and the like are not contrary emotions, being powers of the mind and not emotions. C2 reads "contraries" the same way, as contrary emotions.
# P4 (S6, "general definition") and P5 (S7, "general properties") restate one claim. The wording differs, but what would make it true is the same.
